#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# mixed_fraction_parts

#% text
# `mixed_fraction_parts(x)` gives the pair `[ip, fp]` of the integer part and the fractional part of `x`, both with the sign of `x`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `ip + fp` equals `x`.

#% item
# For a complex number the real and the imaginary part are split separately and recombined.

#% item
# The function maps over lists.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
mixed_fraction_parts(2.7)
#% output
#= [2.0, 0.7000000000000002]

#% cell
mixed_fraction_parts(14/3)
#% output
#= [4, 2/3]

#% cell
mixed_fraction_parts([-5/3, 5/3, 4])
#% output
#= [[-1, -2/3], [1, 2/3], [4, 0]]

#% cell
mixed_fraction_parts(17/(1 + 3*im))
#% output
#= [1 - 5im, 7/10 + -im/10]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `integer_part`, `fractional_part`, `floor`, `round`
